            <ArticleTitle>Circumferential strut fracture as a mechanism of &quot;crush&quot; bifurcation restenosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>770-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.amjcard.2012.11.030</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0002-9149(12)02463-0</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The &quot;Crush&quot; procedure is a 2-stent technique for the treatment of bifurcation lesions with greater rates of in-stent restenosis than the Culotte technique. In conclusion, we report a possible mechanism for this discrepancy in the case of severe Crush stent fracture with associated focal restenosis identified by postmortem microcomputed tomography and histologic examination.</AbstractText>
